   "issue": "The docstring says the twist-two neutral bilinear \"is a bilinear `\u03c8bar_+ \u03b3^+ \u03c8_+` in good quark fields\", but the statement's RHS is `O = {quarkBar .good, quark .good}`, which records no Dirac structure and so equally covers `\u03c8bar_+ \u03b3^+ \u03b3_5 \u03c8_+` and `\u03c8bar_+ i\u03c3^{+i} \u03b3_5 \u03c8_+`. Same problem at line 448, where the trilinear case is written as `\u03c8bar_+ \u03b3^+ F^{+i} \u03c8_+`. This contradicts the module docstring (line 32: \"the Dirac and colour structure contracting them do not enter the grading\") and the module's own summary of these two theorems (lines 69-75), which correctly say only \"a bilinear in good quark fields\".",
